TEXT 64 272 Left 2 ;1. TWO-POLE ANTI-ALIAS FILTER AND BUFFER
TEXT 792 272 Left 2 ;2. GAIN STAGE AND ADC DRIVER
TEXT 784 512 Left 2 ;3. CLOCKED SAMPLE-AND-HOLD PLUS ADC LOAD
TEXT 1328 576 Left 2 ;4. TRACK-ERROR OBSERVER
TEXT 64 304 Left 1 ;Rsrc is source impedance. Each 1k/100p pole is about 1.59 MHz; together they produce an approximately 1.02 MHz -3 dB bandwidth.
TEXT 64 328 Left 1 ;Eiso is a unity-gain ideal buffer: it prevents the second RC section from loading and shifting the first pole.
TEXT 792 304 Left 1 ;Egain models 1.6 V/V front-end gain. Rout, Cload, and Rload model the ADC driver and board/input loading.
TEXT 784 784 Left 1 ;Clock high closes Ssample so CHOLD follows afe. Clock low opens it; CHOLD plus CADC retain the sample while Rleak creates droop.
TEXT 1328 784 Left 1 ;Berror exposes hold minus afe so the acquisition error can be measured directly without changing the signal path.
TEXT 64 824 Left 2 !.param RAA1=1k RAA2=1k CAA1=100p CAA2=100p GAIN=1.6 ROUT=50 CLOAD=50p RSW=25 CHOLD=47p CADC=50p\n.model SAMPLE SW(Ron={RSW} Roff=1G Vt=1.65 Vh=0.1)\n.tran 0 2u 0 2n
TEXT 64 920 Left 2 ;Educational nominal schematic for mixed_signal_daq_transient.cir. The automation substitutes the braced parameters for statistical samples and light/heavy CADC corners.
TEXT 64 952 Left 2 ;For the companion AC study, Vsig becomes AC 1, Vclk is held at 0 V, and the same analog path is swept from 1 kHz to 100 MHz.
